            <div xml:id="d1019">

                <pb facs="1145" n="1135" sameAs="frus:frus1944v04/pg1135"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.24/9–744: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Harriman</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-09-16T18:00:00-04:00">September 16,
                            1944—6 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2220. Reference your 3364 of September 7. The extent to which the Department
                    wishes to insist on the Soviet Government’s agreement to the Department’s <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Aide-Mémoire</hi> of July 6 is still under
                    consideration. The Department suggests, therefore, that if you feel it
                    desirable, you inquire of the Soviet Government, without discussing the contents
                    of the <hi rendition="#italic">Aide-Mémoire</hi>, when a reply may be
                    expected.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
